# File Annotation Headers

All MAJOR files must have an annotation block at the top (after imports). Major files include: page files, layout files, components, hooks, utilities, API routes, type definitions, validation schemas, and content files.

Skip annotations for: barrel exports (index.ts that just re-export), config files, and trivial one-liner files.

## Format

Place this block as a comment immediately after the import statements:

```typescript
/**
 * What this does: [One-line description of the file's purpose]
 * Why it's here: [What problem it solves or what part of the app needs it]
 * How it works: [Brief explanation of the approach/logic — 1-3 sentences]
 * Dependencies: [Key packages or internal modules this file relies on]
 */
```

## Example — A component file

```typescript
import { motion } from "motion/react";
import { cn } from "@repo/utils";

/**
 * What this does: Animated hero section with text reveal and CTA buttons
 * Why it's here: First thing visitors see — sets the tone for the brand
 * How it works: Uses Motion for staggered text animation on mount,
 *   aurora background from Aceternity for the ambient effect,
 *   and a responsive two-column layout with CTA buttons.
 * Dependencies: motion, @repo/ui (Button), @repo/tokens (colors)
 */
export function HeroSection() {
  // ...
}
```

## Example — A utility file

```typescript
import { clsx, type ClassValue } from "clsx";
import { twMerge } from "tailwind-merge";

/**
 * What this does: Merges Tailwind CSS classes with conflict resolution
 * Why it's here: Prevents duplicate/conflicting Tailwind classes in dynamic components
 * How it works: Combines clsx for conditional classes with tailwind-merge for deduplication
 * Dependencies: clsx, tailwind-merge
 */
export function cn(...inputs: ClassValue[]) {
  return twMerge(clsx(inputs));
}
```

## Rules

- Keep each field to 1-2 lines max. Be concise, not verbose.
- For Dependencies, list the most important ones — no need to list React itself.
- When creating or substantially editing a major file, add or update the annotation.
- Do NOT add annotations to files that are just barrel exports or configs.
